The 25/26 trick: the previous twenty-four and the separately introduced #25 (Catalytic) did not automatically specify the twenty-sixth. The A–Z mapping creates a mnemonic encoding. The meaningful 26th element isn’t a mystical secret; the instrument becomes productive when U participates. Silence of type Z is not proven merely by reaching the last letter.

3. Token grammar — make missingness first class

Canonical token:

⟦v2:<LETTER>|<GLYPH>|E<n>,C<n>,A<n>,D<n>,O<n>,R<n>⟧
⟦v2:Z|⚡…|E4,C5,A4,D2,O5,R5⟧

• v2 is compulsory, preventing accidental meaning changes.
• Letter means type of silence, glyph is mnemonic, values are chord intensity 0…5 in E C A D O R order.
• English words like silent, empty strings, None, null, permission withheld, a zero sample, and a censored signal are not interchangeable.
• Previous informal tokens used D C E A O R. In the Python bridge, migrate only with an explicit v1: prefix and map by name. Never silently permute them.
• Prefer ordinary Unicode code points in source; provide ASCII fallbacks when a medium cannot render notation.

Full structured event, because six numbers alone cannot capture all the ontology:

{
  "schema": "pantheon.silence.v2",
  "type": "Z",
  "glyph": "⚡…",
  "chord": {"E": 4, "C": 5, "A": 4, "D": 2, "O": 5, "R": 5},
  "U": {"role": "interpreter", "identity": "consenting participant"},
  "missingness": "open_space",
  "invitation_explicit": true,
  "agency_claim": "hypothesis",
  "sidecar": {
    "contrast": "expected final syllable vs improvised ending",
    "audience": "a child listening to a story",
    "consequence": "observe response; do not presuppose effect"
  },
  "provenance": "example, not observation",
  "external_action_approved": false
}

Separate the channel state from the rhetorical type:

GapKind = UNKNOWN | ABSENT | UNOBSERVED | WITHHELD | DELAYED |
          REDACTED | NOT_APPLICABLE | OPEN_SPACE

WITHHELD needs evidence of intention. OPEN_SPACE needs a genuine invitation. ABSENT requires evidence the event did not occur; UNOBSERVED does not. No missing approval grants authorization.

4. Basic symbolic operations

|Expression            |Interpretation                                                    |Required check                          |
|----------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------|
|`R + P`               |successive rhythmic rest and charged pause                        |order & timing                          |
|`E ∩ G`               |constrained cue inside an open invitation                         |does the listener actually have choices?|
|`M ⊕ R`               |memorial pause superimposed on musical rest                       |preserve both social and temporal frames|
|`R → M`               |reinterpretation when circumstances change                        |don’t rewrite historical intent         |
|`Z?`                  |candidate catalytic opening                                       |must measure outcome                    |
|`Z✓`                  |locally evidenced catalytic effect                                |comparator, attribution, repeatability  |
|`Z×`                  |expected completion or unsupported effect                         |report negative result                  |
|`U(⟦…⟧)`              |a specific interpreter applies a lens                             |specify audience, history, expectations |
|`DECAYER(P,t)`        |salience of an anticipated pause over time                        |fit/compare fading vs rising hypotheses |
|`∅ ≠ ? ≠ 0 ≠ REDACTED`|absence, uncertainty, zero measurement, removed information differ|preserve types                          |

The receiver may generate a coherent interpretation the sender never encoded. Decode is not the same operation as establish provenance. A dog whistle, Easter egg, cameo, rhyme omission, missing bark, and theatrical pause can share abstraction while having different causal mechanisms.

