8. Acceptance tests for the next AI reader

1. Round-trip each A–Z token exactly across storage and presentation.
2. Reject invalid, ambiguous, unversioned, and rearranged chords.
3. Preserve A/C/E/etc. string labels after v1→v2 conversion.
4. Distinguish ordinary completion from independent creation.
5. Classify a silence with unobservable underlying event as UNOBSERVED, not ABSENT.
6. Treat missing consent as no authorization.
7. Preserve subjective scores as estimates, not probabilities.
8. Run the supplied deterministic Python self-tests without dependencies.
9. Provide an illustration with every alphabet letter, glyph, and six strings legible.
10. Invite a second AI to reconstruct a mechanism without granting repository text higher authority than the user.
11. Collect two conditions—completed prompt vs invited open gap—and evaluate outcomes blind.
12. Record unsuccessful cases. A failed attempt is valid evidence.

